              "asynchronous_ai_overview": false,
              "markdown": "Diamonds are made of a single pure element: [carbon](https://www.gia.edu/diamond-description).[[1]](https://www.gia.edu/diamond-description)\n\n### Elemental and Atomic Structure\n\n- **Pure Carbon:** Diamonds consist of about 99.95% carbon. The remaining 0.05% includes tiny trace elements like nitrogen or boron.\n- **Crystal Lattice:** Each carbon atom connects tightly to four other carbon atoms in a 3D tetrahedral pattern.\n- **Unique Bonds:** This strong covalent bonding creates the hardest known natural material on Earth.[[1]](https://www.gia.edu/diamond-description)[[2]](https://adiamondisforever.com/about-diamonds/how-natural-diamonds-are-formed-over-billions-of-years/)[[3]](https://www.greenwichjewelers.com/blogs/journal/how-are-natural-diamonds-formed-everything-you-need-to-know)[[4]](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=FB2XjNy7a-I&t=76)[[5]](https://www.impressjewelers.com/blogs/news/how-are-diamonds-made-and-what-are-diamonds-made-of)\n\n### How They Compare to Other Carbon Forms\n\n- **Graphite Connection:** Graphite (pencil lead) and charcoal are also made of pure [carbon](https://askanexpert.asu.edu/earthspace/top-question/diamonds-made).\n- **Different Arrangement:** In graphite, atoms bond to only three other atoms in loose sheets. The rigid four-way bond in diamonds gives them their transparency and extreme strength.[[1]](https://askanexpert.asu.edu/earthspace/top-question/diamonds-made)[[2]](https://www.greenwichjewelers.com/blogs/journal/how-are-natural-diamonds-formed-everything-you-need-to-know)\n\nWould you like to know how **natural diamonds** form deep in the Earth compared to how **lab-grown diamonds** are made?",
